      "title": "Reading the Place Names Carefully",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_2",
          "text": "Keeping the chapter\u2019s own place names in view prevents a familiar modern map from being treated as the only possible route. The geographical uncertainty does not erase the text\u2019s setting; it distinguishes the named route in the narrative from later attempts to match every location with a modern site.",
          "verse_refs": [
