    },
    {
      "kind": "surrounding_passages",
      "title": "Exodus as a Larger Story",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_3",
          "text": "Exodus 14 is a climactic deliverance scene, but the book does not end with escape from Egypt. Exodus moves from oppression and deliverance to covenant, covenant breach and renewal, the construction of the tabernacle, and the arrival of divine glory. Reading these movements together keeps the sea crossing within the book\u2019s larger account rather than treating departure from Egypt as its endpoint.",
